# L §8.4 and L §5.14 Legs: a leg's place is a place, or a hole of a place type; a none place is refused (RUN-NONE),
# and a refused movement whose place isn't known could book into any place, so a place's flows can't leave it out in
# silence: flows of either candidate place is refused, as a balance is. (Was: 0.00 PLN, the movement left out of
# flows; found with the fault of L5_5_axis_picks_leg_place.)
=== m.tally
model p14
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index people = [ana, ben]

place pln[p in people]: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input dest: key people
input amt: money PLN
input pay_day: date

move gift: transfers
  on pay_day
  leg cash from world to pln[dest] amount amt

ask q: flows(pln[p], 2026) for p in people law 2026-06-30
ask b: bal(pln[ana], 2026-12-31) law 2026-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  dest = none
  amt = 10.00 PLN
  pay_day = 2026-03-01
  opening[pln[ana]] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[pln[ben]] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
=== expect
b: refused: RUN-NONE ...
...
q (p = ana): refused: RUN-NONE ...
...
q (p = ben): refused: RUN-NONE ...
...
